<ol class="ltx_toclist ltx_toclist_subsection">
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsubsection"><a href="#S5.SS2.SSS1" title="In V-B RQ2: Code-Specific versus Generic LLMs ‣ V Results ‣ Evaluating Large Language Models for Functional and Maintainable Code in Industrial Settings: A Case Study at ASML" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref"><span class="ltx_text">V-B</span>1 </span>Match-based metrics</span></a></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsubsection"><a href="#S5.SS2.SSS2" title="In V-B RQ2: Code-Specific versus Generic LLMs ‣ V Results ‣ Evaluating Large Language Models for Functional and Maintainable Code in Industrial Settings: A Case Study at ASML" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref"><span class="ltx_text">V-B</span>2 </span>Execution-based metrics</span></a></li>
</ol></li>
<li class="ltx_tocentry ltx_tocentry_subsection"><a href="#S5.SS3" title="In V Results ‣ Evaluating Large Language Models for Functional and Maintainable Code in Industrial Settings: A Case Study at ASML" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_title"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_ref"><span class="ltx_text">V-C</span> </span><span class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">RQ3: Model Size</span></span></a>
